<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="ArchiFabric" id="id-53dd07a57c7c4111904e34eaabca33f6" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-e4bfad150ea64059b034d9c4b01b0266" type="strategy">
    <folder name="Value Streams" id="id-71cd3e433f184db995a9f92e41d1e88a">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Deliver Customer Value" id="id-a16fb70b0fb64c1bbfdcc6620eecc03b">
        <documentation>Deliver Customer Value represents the complete journey through which the organization creates and delivers value to its customers. It connects customer needs with the development, delivery and ongoing support of products and services.

The value stream provides an end-to-end perspective across organizational boundaries. It consists of the value streams **Understand Customer Needs**, **Develop Customer Solution**, **Deliver Customer Solution** and **Support Customer**.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Creates value for customers by understanding their needs, developing suitable solutions, delivering services and providing ongoing support."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Understand Customer Needs" id="id-4ae273cbb2534ee3bedb680a4dc19a86">
        <documentation>Understand Customer Needs focuses on gaining a clear understanding of what customers need, expect and experience. Information is collected from customer interactions, feedback, market developments and other relevant sources.

These insights provide the foundation for developing products and services that create customer value. They also help the organization identify opportunities to improve existing solutions and the overall customer experience.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Creates insight into customer needs, expectations and experiences as a basis for developing appropriate solutions."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Develop Customer Solution" id="id-0aa4bf2ad27d400f8ed0fc352e8051e8">
        <documentation>Develop Customer Solution transforms identified customer needs into solutions that can be delivered by the organization. This includes defining requirements, designing the solution and developing or adapting the necessary products, services and software.

Development is performed iteratively where appropriate, allowing customer feedback and new insights to be incorporated. The resulting solution should be both valuable to the customer and feasible for the organization to deliver and maintain.</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Transforms customer needs into products, services and software solutions that can be delivered to customers."/>
        <property key="Lead" value="5000"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Deliver Customer Solution" id="id-de535385b8a84def8a4c9275ef3f943d">
        <documentation>Deliver Customer Value represents the complete journey through which the organization creates and delivers value to its customers. It connects customer needs with the development, delivery and ongoing support of products and services.

The value stream provides an end-to-end perspective across organizational boundaries. It consists of the value streams **Understand Customer Needs**, **Develop Customer Solution**, **Deliver Customer Solution** and **Support Customer**.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Provides the agreed solution to the customer and ensures that it can be successfully used."/>
        <property key="Lead" value="2500"/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Support Customer" id="id-ccf1e195f33f4ab88bac3942ebe518e3">
        <documentation>Support Customer helps customers use delivered products and services effectively. Support may include answering questions, resolving incidents, providing guidance and handling requests for assistance.

Customer interactions during support also provide valuable feedback about products and services. These insights can be used to improve both the customer experience and future solutions, creating a feedback loop to **Understand Customer Needs**.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Supports customers in the effective use of delivered products and services and resolves questions or problems."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Conclude Customer Engagement" id="id-10e9cb2db2b34fd187f0816ca3de5e85">
        <documentation>Conclude Customer Engagement focuses on the orderly termination of products, services, or customer relationships when they are no longer required or appropriate. This includes managing cancellations, fulfilling contractual obligations, transferring or returning customer information, and ensuring that services are discontinued in a controlled and transparent manner.

The value stream ensures that the final stage of the customer journey is handled with the same care and professionalism as its earlier stages. By respecting customer interests, regulatory requirements, and data protection obligations, the organization maintains trust even after the relationship has ended. Insights gained from customer departures can also contribute to improving products, services, and the overall customer experience.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Capabilities" id="id-0045e3d7afba4bcfa920459519441f32">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Customer Relationship Management" id="id-89672d9defb746a899f5b4993742dbf5">
        <documentation>Customer Relationship Management enables the organization to manage its relationships and interactions with customers throughout the customer lifecycle. It provides insight into customers, contacts, agreements, interactions and commercial opportunities.

The capability supports consistent and coordinated customer interactions across organizational functions. It helps build sustainable relationships by ensuring that relevant customer information is available when decisions are made or services are delivered.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Ability to establish, maintain and develop effective relationships with customers."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Customer experience management (CXM)" id="id-4247a7c8d3a746509f49a623fc194b0c">
        <documentation>Customer Experience Management (CXM) enables the organization to understand how customers experience its products, services and interactions. It combines customer feedback, behavioral information and other insights to create a coherent view of the customer experience.

The capability supports continuous improvement of customer journeys and interactions. It helps the organization identify customer expectations, recognize areas for improvement and make informed decisions that increase customer value and satisfaction.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Ability to understand, manage and improve customer experiences across all interactions with the organization."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Software Development" id="id-30584da1cf50425aa387c3cc7e051b0a">
        <documentation>Software Development enables the organization to translate requirements into reliable and maintainable software solutions. It includes activities such as software design, development, testing, integration and deployment.

The capability supports both the development of new solutions and the continuous improvement of existing software. Development practices should enable the organization to respond effectively to changing customer needs while maintaining appropriate levels of quality, security and maintainability.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Ability to design, develop, test and maintain software solutions that support customer and organizational needs."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Service Delivery" id="id-a7c1d2ab54624442b7a8bbd9818444ba">
        <documentation>Service Delivery enables the organization to provide products and services to customers in a controlled and predictable manner. It coordinates the people, processes, information and technology required to fulfil customer commitments.

The capability focuses on ensuring that delivered services meet agreed expectations regarding quality, availability and performance. Effective service delivery connects organizational capabilities with the value that customers actually receive.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Ability to deliver products and services to customers according to agreed requirements and service levels."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Customer Support" id="id-387f7e58454e4cf6a5edf8ee72c9f938">
        <documentation>Customer Support enables the organization to assist customers before, during and after the delivery of products and services. It includes handling questions, service requests, incidents and other forms of customer assistance.

The capability contributes directly to the customer experience by providing timely and effective support. Information obtained through customer support can also reveal recurring problems and opportunities for improving products, services and customer interactions.
</documentation>
        <property key="Definition" value="Ability to assist customers and resolve questions, requests and problems related to products and services."/>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Standards Library" id="id-0e06328a4500483bb09584c72271e57c">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Value Stream" id="id-637aea4ad2924b78931b122bf16839ea">
        <documentation>A value stream represents a sequence of activities that create an overall result for a customer, stakeholder, or end user.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Capability" id="id-cacf1134ff204690b265ded6e0340d6b">
        <documentation>A capability represents an ability that an active structure element, such as an organization, person, or system, possesses.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Course of Action" id="id-0337cb5e928f48b2bf66c3b9de831f92">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:CourseOfAction" name="Improve Customer Engagement" id="id-fe4d2f6c12a24ed4a6f3e3fba39909c1">
        <documentation>Conclude Customer Engagement</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-5907d1bf2e7f491e954fce6cf56921b5" type="business">
    <folder name="Standards Library" id="id-fde9b0ad72ae4a96abbd905ad1b98452"/>
    <folder name="Documentation" id="id-5820d46412bc45319493e74b6984dff9">
      <folder name="Installing ArchiFabric" id="id-1f7111b41635475d8bcce94b6f654eed">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Download the Suite" id="id-bc7a6e4ea97e48fb8ab32aea82f9a9c8">
          <documentation>ArchiFabric is distributed as an open-source project via GitHub. The most recent, stable version of the suite is always available for download from the official Releases page.

**Steps to download:**

1. Navigate to the official ArchiFabric Releases page: [https://github.com/Optiprise/archi-fabric/releases](https://github.com/Optiprise/archi-fabric/releases).
2. Look for the version at the top of the page marked with the green **Latest** label.
3. Expand the **Assets** section at the bottom of the release notes.

You will find two different ZIP files here. It is important to choose the package that matches your operating system, as the underlying PDF generator (WeasyPrint) is system-specific.

* **ArchiFabric-[version]-Windows.zip** *(Recommended for Windows)*
This is a complete, standalone bundle for Windows users. In addition to the ArchiFabric scripts, this package contains a *pre-compiled* version of WeasyPrint. The major advantage of this bundle is that PDF generation works out of the box, without the need to install Python or deal with strict corporate firewalls blocking downloads during execution.
* **ArchiFabric-[version]-Generic.zip** *(For macOS &amp; Linux)*
This package exclusively contains the clean ArchiFabric scripts. Because package management varies greatly across macOS and Linux, WeasyPrint is not included here. You can easily install WeasyPrint on these systems yourself via the terminal (see the next section for instructions).

**What's next?**
Download the ZIP file that applies to your system to your local computer (e.g., your `Downloads` folder). Do *not* extract the file just yet; in the next step (2.1.3), we will explain exactly how to correctly integrate these files into your Archi environment.</documentation>
          <property key="Reference" value="[GitHub](https://github.com/Optiprise/archi-fabric)"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="Prerequisites" id="id-d1773676f4e04009b7b377b2e9d4acb1">
          <documentation>Before ArchiFabric can be used, you need to ensure that a few foundational tools are installed on your system:

* **Archi:** The core modeling environment itself. You can download the latest version from the [Archi download page](https://www.archimatetool.com/download/).
* **jArchi Plugin:** This plugin provides the scripting engine that powers ArchiFabric. Currently, the jArchi plugin is available exclusively to Patreon supporters of the Archi project. We highly recommend becoming a Patreon member—not only to gain access to this essential plugin, but also to support the continued software development and maintenance of Archi. You can find more information here: [jArchi Plugin](https://www.archimatetool.com/plugins/#jArchi).
* **WeasyPrint:** The rendering engine used to convert the generated HTML into high-quality PDFs. You can find the latest releases on their [GitHub page](https://github.com/Kozea/WeasyPrint/releases) and documentation on [Weasyprint documentation hub](https://doc.courtbouillon.org/weasyprint/stable/first_steps.html#installation).
* *For Linux and macOS:* WeasyPrint is generally available through your native package manager and can be installed system-wide.
* *For Windows:* You can download the provided ZIP file. In a later phase, a standalone `.exe` file may be included directly within the ArchiFabric folder for a smoother installation experience.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Extract and Install ArchiFabric" id="id-8edc94ba834546d98aa880f90b56615e">
          <documentation>Now that you have downloaded the correct ZIP file for your operating system, the next step is to integrate the suite into Archi's scripting environment. Archi uses a dedicated folder to store and execute jArchi scripts. We will extract the files and place them directly into this folder.

**Installation Steps:**

1. **Locate the Scripts Folder:** Open the Archi application. In the top menu, navigate to **Window > Scripts Manager** to open the Scripts panel. In this panel, click the **Show in System Explorer** button (the folder icon). This will open the exact directory on your computer where Archi expects its scripts to be located (usually `Documents/Archi/scripts`).
2. **Extract the ZIP Archive:** Locate the `ArchiFabric-[version].zip` file you downloaded in the previous step and extract its contents. You should now see a folder named `archifabric-pdf`.
3. **Move the Folder:** Copy or move this entire `archifabric-pdf` folder directly into the Archi scripts folder you opened in step 1.  
    _**Important:** Ensure you move the complete folder, keeping its internal structure intact. The correct path on your system should look something like this: `.../scripts/archifabric-pdf/archifabric-pdf.ajs`._


4. **Refresh Archi:** Return to the Archi application and click the **Refresh** button in the Scripts Manager panel.

The `archifabric-pdf` folder will now appear in your Scripts Manager tree, and the suite is officially installed in your Archi environment!</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Disable CommonJS Support" id="id-8021ef59d01348eeaa8351983d349747">
          <documentation>To ensure ArchiFabric runs smoothly, you must adjust a specific setting in the jArchi preferences. ArchiFabric uses modern JavaScript ES modules (`.mjs` files), which conflict with jArchi's legacy CommonJS module system if both are active simultaneously.

**Configuration Steps:**

1. Open the Archi **Preferences** window:
	* **Windows / Linux:** Navigate to **Edit > Preferences** in the top menu.
	* **macOS:** Navigate to **Archi > Settings** (or Preferences) in the top menu bar.
2. In the left-hand menu of the preferences window, select **Scripting**.
3. Locate the **JavaScript** section at the bottom of the right-hand panel.
4. Ensure the checkbox next to **Enable CommonJS Support** is **unchecked** (empty).
5. Click **Apply and Close** to save your changes.

_**Note:** If this option remains checked, the jArchi engine will fail to load ArchiFabric's modules correctly, which will result in immediate execution errors when trying to generate your document._</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
    </folder>
