  <folder name="Technology &amp; Physical" id="id-3040aba3535d445daea019f3f9c14c5e" type="technology">
    <folder name="archifabric-pdf" id="id-ee93ddc1993b4cd49c3bdffc0167ec48">
      <folder name="artifacts" id="id-27ebe8feca3a4ce6a1e3bed844dbd1ac">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Document.mjs" id="id-ff071a5cbe40422983a0cb5a1895c13a">
          <documentation>The `Document.mjs` module serves as the root rendering artifact within the ArchiFabric engine and inherently extends the abstract `Artifact` base class. Its primary technical responsibility is to construct the main HTML wrapper (typically a `&lt;div>` appended with dynamically parsed CSS classes) that safely encapsulates all subsequent generated markup. During this initialization phase, it also triggers the optional insertion of a front page placeholder via the markup engine.

A key design pattern in its `render(modelElement, targetElement)` method is the strict separation of metadata from visual text. The module explicitly evaluates `modelElement.labelExpression` solely to register the `documentTitle` within the `globalVars` map. Furthermore, it executes a silent expression parsing on the `modelElement.documentation`. This guarantees that any global setters are registered in the engine's memory without their raw string values ever being appended to the actual HTML output.

To process child artifacts, the module instantiates the `ModelStructure` class to retrieve the spatial pairings between templates and their corresponding target data. It implements a robust, recursive helper function named `processTemplateNode`. This function seamlessly dives into nested ArchiMate view references (`archimate-diagram-model`), scanning these modular building blocks specifically for executable `diagram-model-group` elements. It ensures that purely visual view names are ignored, routing only valid artifact nodes to `this.artifactory.render()`.

Finally, the Document module enforces ArchiFabric's contextual data inheritance principles. When processing and routing its nested children, the script evaluates the spatial pairing links. If a child artifact does not have a specific data target explicitly drawn via an ArchiMate relationship, the module ensures that the child safely inherits the `targetElement` context from the root Document, guaranteeing uninterrupted data flow down the execution tree.</documentation>
          <property key="GitHub" value="[archifabric-pdf/artifacts/Document.mjs](https://github.com/Optiprise/archi-fabric/blob/main/archifabric-pdf/artifacts/Document.mjs)"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Catalog.mjs" id="id-eb5c39f9b906477a8f18da0ba9a84271">
          <property key="GitHub" value="https://github.com/Optiprise/archi-fabric/blob/main/archifabric-pdf/artifacts/Catalog.mjs"/>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Diagram.mjs" id="id-9e5ea7b5fff1496f89c0434933587bcc"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Documentation.mjs" id="id-6ff81b03c2f34e7580f664a970d3fd8e"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="CSS.mjs" id="id-7dca23ddae114dfebdd00d29b6c3e99c"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Matrix.mjs" id="id-9a961329dbd841c69cf8263b14a43854"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Section.mjs" id="id-183ee89f07e7465aa0fc2f5d99784449"/>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="TOC.mjs" id="id-fca5faf0ff6a4d5280791a8900b18703"/>
      </folder>
      <folder name="core" id="id-a056a1f615c148e68f324fbc123de1b5">
        <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Artifact.mjs" id="id-238115a915704128976b3a7d9fb75261"/>
