  <folder name="Motivation" id="id-8fa6e0b6c7c947cd9abfd20113ee1cbb" type="motivation">
    <folder name="Business Impact Analysis" id="id-39ce7a9943cb4638bc683842d5192731">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:Assessment" name="Adopting AI" id="id-1de10986886645bdbc757fd98384a643">
        <documentation>The assessment indicates that adopting Artificial Intelligence offers substantial opportunities to improve organizational performance, although the expected benefits vary considerably across business capabilities. The analysis examined potential improvements in productivity, automation, service quality, and customer value. The findings suggest that a selective adoption strategy will deliver greater value than introducing AI uniformly across the organization.

**Customer Experience Management (CXM)** shows limited potential for additional value from AI. Existing customer feedback processes and direct customer interactions already provide sufficient insight into customer expectations and experiences. AI-supported sentiment analysis and customer segmentation could offer incremental improvements, but these benefits are not expected to justify significant investments at this stage. The organization should therefore maintain its current approach while monitoring relevant developments in AI technology.

**Software Development** and **Customer Support** demonstrate the strongest opportunities for AI adoption. Within Software Development, AI-assisted coding, automated testing, and documentation generation are expected to improve developer productivity and reduce development lead times. Customer Support presents even greater potential through intelligent self-service, automated request handling, and AI-assisted incident resolution. These applications could fundamentally improve service accessibility and operational scalability. **Service Delivery** also offers opportunities, particularly in predictive monitoring and operational planning, although its overall potential is assessed as moderate.

Based on these findings, the organization should **prioritize AI initiatives within Customer Support and Software Development**, supported by targeted pilot projects and measurable performance indicators. Service Delivery should be considered for selective improvements where clear operational benefits can be demonstrated. Investments in AI for Customer Experience Management should remain limited until stronger business cases emerge. Successful adoption will require appropriate data governance, security measures, employee involvement, and continuous evaluation of realized business value.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Implementation &amp; Migration" id="id-86a580ceee33412d8a2d06310e413655" type="implementation_migration">
    <folder name="Improve Customer Engagement" id="id-b4ba21aff58241729da9c42a4f50afc6">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:WorkPackage" name="Improve Customer Engagement" id="id-fd484fecbfce48b19b02f9a9c6a3cb7a">
        <documentation>Conclude Customer Engagement</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Other" id="id-142c883e24df4b74ba9293cdf77a0563" type="other"/>
  <folder name="Relations" id="id-6b56709edd674fd49203ca98dc3f8972" type="relations">
    <folder name="BIA" id="id-42c739743d6842a29e54a42472eb4258">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-b4f0ace3a0e9452db8c5f43235ddc632" source="id-4247a7c8d3a746509f49a623fc194b0c" target="id-1de10986886645bdbc757fd98384a643" strength="●○○○○">
        <documentation>AI offers limited additional value to Customer Experience Management in the current organizational context. While AI can support customer sentiment analysis, feedback classification, and the identification of customer preferences, the organization already has effective methods for understanding customer experiences. Furthermore, personal interaction and human interpretation remain essential for understanding complex customer needs. AI may provide incremental improvements, but its overall contribution is expected to be relatively small.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-783f4fe6bcc042bfa719529a42feb56c" source="id-30584da1cf50425aa387c3cc7e051b0a" target="id-1de10986886645bdbc757fd98384a643" strength="●●●○○">
        <documentation>AI has significant potential to improve Software Development by assisting developers with code generation, testing, documentation, and code reviews. AI-powered development tools can reduce repetitive work, accelerate delivery, and help identify software defects earlier in the development process. Although human oversight remains essential for architecture, security, and quality assurance, the expected productivity gains make Software Development a strong candidate for AI adoption.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-9cdc9803f2de4c46a1105b389617992f" source="id-a7c1d2ab54624442b7a8bbd9818444ba" target="id-1de10986886645bdbc757fd98384a643" strength="●●○○○">
        <documentation>AI can provide moderate added value to Service Delivery through improved planning, automated operational activities, and predictive analysis. AI-supported monitoring may help identify potential service disruptions, optimize resource allocation, and improve operational efficiency. However, many service delivery activities depend on established processes, existing systems, and contractual obligations. Consequently, the expected benefits are meaningful but concentrated in specific operational activities rather than across the entire capability.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:InfluenceRelationship" id="id-774838709ad44e75bb7a4382d0ff3a20" source="id-387f7e58454e4cf6a5edf8ee72c9f938" target="id-1de10986886645bdbc757fd98384a643" strength="●●●●○">
        <documentation>AI has transformative potential for Customer Support by enabling intelligent self-service, automated request handling, and continuous assistance outside regular business hours. AI-powered virtual assistants can answer frequently asked questions, suggest solutions, summarize customer interactions, and support employees in resolving complex incidents. By combining automation with human expertise, the organization can significantly improve response times, scalability, and service consistency while allowing support employees to focus on situations requiring personal attention.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Deliver Customer Value" id="id-664efc522f7a404c9097983637478e06">
