          <documentation>Setting up ArchiFabric is a straightforward process consisting of three main phases: downloading the appropriate release package for your operating system from GitHub, extracting and moving the suite into your local Archi scripts directory, and configuring the jArchi preferences to ensure compatibility with modern JavaScript modules. Follow the detailed steps below to get your environment ready for automated document generation.</documentation>
          <property key="Lead" value="Before you can start weaving your architecture models into cohesive documents, you need to set up ArchiFabric within your Archi environment. ArchiFabric runs on top of the jArchi scripting engine and utilizes external open-source tools to generate high-quality PDFs."/>
        </element>
