          <documentation>The **Document** artifact acts as the foundational wrapper for your entire ArchiFabric report. By serving as the root container on your canvas, it dictates where the publication begins and ends. Every visual element, section, or matrix that you nest spatially inside this container will be systematically compiled into a single, cohesive PDF document.

Configuring this root artifact is straightforward and visually intuitive. By setting the **Name** property to `Document`, you instruct the engine to use this specific module. The **Label Expression** plays a crucial role here: the text you provide in this field (for example, `My First Document`) is automatically extracted to define the final filename of your generated PDF, as well as establishing the global title of the report.

Additionally, the Document artifact allows you to orchestrate global settings without cluttering your visual output. You can use the artifact's **Documentation** field to silently set global variables—such as authors, versions, or reference links—using standard expression tags (e.g., `${set:Author:John Doe}`). The engine will parse these variables in the background, making them available throughout your entire report, while keeping the main document perfectly clean. You can also append parameters like `class=&lt;classname>` to the Name field to apply custom CSS styling to the overall document wrapper.</documentation>
        </element>
