          <bounds x="148" y="312" width="156" height="25"/>
          <content>Hello World!</content>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-bbb982237e2f481c8c01c33d57f3eece" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="148" y="276" width="156" height="25"/>
          <content>Diagram</content>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-928fc3e0a804444c84586a32609cef60" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="0" borderType="2">
          <bounds x="28" y="312" width="120" height="25"/>
          <content>Label Expression:</content>
        </child>
        <documentation>We will use two new Artifacts for this: **Documentation** (to extract the written description of the view) and **Diagram** (to extract the visual image itself).

Follow these steps to link your architecture directly:

1. **Add a Documentation Artifact:** Drag a new **Group** element *inside* your existing `Section` group. In the Properties panel, set its **Name** to `Documentation`.
2. **Link the Text Target:** Locate the `Deliver Customer Value` view in the **Architecture** folder of your model tree. Drag this view and drop it directly *inside* the `Documentation` group.
3. **Add a Diagram Artifact:** Drag another **Group** element inside your `Section` group, placing it below the Documentation group. Set its **Name** to `Diagram`.
4. **Link the Image Target:** Drag the exact same `Deliver Customer Value` view from the model tree directly *inside* this new `Diagram` group.
5. **Adjust the Diagram Size:** Resize the nested view element you just dropped inside the `Diagram` group. ArchiFabric uses the physical width of this element on your canvas to determine the relative width of the diagram in the final PDF. Try making it slightly narrower than the group itself.
6. **Generate the Output:** Run the ArchiFabric script again and save the file.

When you open the updated PDF, your &quot;Hello World!&quot; chapter will now automatically display the textual description of the Deliver Customer Value architecture, immediately followed by the rendered diagram image. Because you adjusted the width of the view element on the canvas, you will see that the diagram image is scaled proportionally in your document!</documentation>
        <property key="Lead" value="A document is only as valuable as the data it presents. We will now expand our &quot;Hello World&quot; document by pulling in real architectural data. We will use the **Deliver Customer Value** view from the **Architecture** folder, which maps a customer value stream to its underlying business capabilities."/>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="Apply the View Artifact" id="id-1dd7c4a2f3734fe0afb43a60c1b916e1">
