            <bounds x="109" y="144" width="291" height="35"/>
          </child>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-695c0d213ca949fb9dfba7c173001f34" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#f6f5f4" alpha="64" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="24" y="168" width="284" height="49"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
          <sourceConnection id="id-f28c42bc3e2b4f9bba4d47aa523fd053" lineWidth="2" lineColor="#1a5fb4" source="id-695c0d213ca949fb9dfba7c173001f34" target="id-0aad82586c104189a5216b1c88374279" type="1"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-8ddeb4ea40ee4d04ba7090d8a2d7ded4" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="0" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="36" y="180" width="265" height="25"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
          <content>Step 3. Link the Template</content>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-f70cb513e39145ebbd0c94cdeb8d4024" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#f6f5f4" alpha="64" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="24" y="228" width="284" height="49"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-2183e71436984061a6389a6a03e49d12" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="0" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="36" y="240" width="265" height="25"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
          <sourceConnection id="id-2234e43684c642e098a420dc754f752e" lineWidth="2" lineColor="#1a5fb4" source="id-2183e71436984061a6389a6a03e49d12" target="id-abf85f7d39ba429fa1530f71b8eee5d8" type="1">
            <bendpoint startX="384" endX="-122" endY="55"/>
          </sourceConnection>
          <content>Step 4. Link the Target</content>
        </child>
        <documentation>By placing a target view immediately after our template view on the document canvas, we create a **TargetStructure**. This simple but powerful pairing tells ArchiFabric to automatically push the target's content—such as its name, documentation, and diagram—through the layout we defined in the previous step.

**Follow these steps to apply your template:**

1. Open your `My First Document` canvas again.
2. To clean up, **delete** the hardcoded `Documentation` and `Diagram` groups you created in earlier exercises.
3. **Link the Template:** Drag your newly created `View Artifacts` view from the model tree directly *inside* your document's main `Section` group.
4. **Link the Target:** Drag the `Deliver Customer Value` view from the **Architecture** folder and drop it *inside* the exact same group, placing it right next to or below the template view. This combination forms our *TargetStructure*.
5. **Generate the Output:** Run the ArchiFabric script again and save your file.

When you open the generated PDF, you will see a new dynamic sub-header titled **&quot;Deliver Customer Value&quot;**, followed by the documentation and the correctly scaled diagram image. The underlying setup is now fully dynamic: ArchiFabric recognized the TargetStructure pattern and automatically resolved the `${name}` expression to the target's actual name!</documentation>
        <property key="Lead" value="Now that we have created a reusable layout template (our ModelStructure), it is time to put it to work. In this section, we will apply the template to our actual architectural data."/>
      </element>
