        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-ff0f37a423ce4d238731879611de6534" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="148" y="24" width="156" height="25"/>
          <content>Document</content>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-1fd701b568e44876a0c7d99c03ec91eb" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="148" y="60" width="156" height="25"/>
          <content>My First Document</content>
        </child>
        <documentation>Now that you understand the basic principles, let's put the visual engine into practice by creating a simple &quot;Hello World&quot; document. In this exercise, we will use two core Artifacts: a **Document** and a **Section**.

Follow these steps to build your first report visually:

1. **Create the Root Artifact:** Drag a standard **Group** (Visual Group) onto your Archi canvas.
2. **Assign the Module:** In the Properties view, set the **Name** of this group to `Document`. This tells the ArchiFabric engine to treat this container as the main document wrapper.
3. **Set the Document Title:** Set the **Label Expression** of this group to `My First Document`. For a Document artifact, this expression automatically determines the generated PDF's filename and the global document title.
4. **Nest a Chapter:** Drag a second **Group** and drop it *inside* the Document group to nest it spatially.
5. **Assign the Child Module:** Set the **Name** of this nested group to `Section`.
6. **Set the Chapter Heading:** Set the **Label Expression** of this nested group to `Hello World!`. For a Section artifact, this expression generates a formatted chapter heading (e.g., an `&lt;h1>` HTML tag).
7. **Generate the Output:** Run the ArchiFabric script from your Archi Scripts menu.

> Within seconds, ArchiFabric will compile your visual structure and generate a PDF file named **My First Document.pdf**. When you open it, you will see a clean, formatted document containing your very first chapter titled **Hello World!**.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="Enriching with Custom Text and Markdown" id="id-eeda05bb14e748e2ba17460dcfe0e160">
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Group" id="id-134637307ee04fbaac1df209d300918f" name="Document" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="64">
          <bounds x="420" y="36" width="400" height="301"/>
          <feature name="labelExpression" value="My First Document"/>
          <feature name="lineAlpha" value="64"/>
          <child xsi:type="archimate:Group" id="id-09c0c02015a94757bd39a682fa512bf0" name="Section" targetConnections="id-65084328549848f0a1556784f0a149b5" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1">
            <bounds y="60" width="400" height="49"/>
            <feature name="labelExpression" value="Hello World!"/>
            <documentation>**Welcome** to our first ArchiFabric document. This section demonstrates how a _Label Expression_ creates a header, while this text is placed directly beneath it.</documentation>
          </child>
          <child xsi:type="archimate:Group" id="id-0b08adbc4ebc41d19908f09424679353" name="Section" targetConnections="id-d6654e8d9a0d400ab128dd2b72e8d8c9" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1">
            <bounds y="144" width="400" height="49"/>
            <documentation>*Note: Because this Section has no Label Expression, it renders as a clean text block without a header. This makes it perfect for custom styling later.*</documentation>
          </child>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-52f21087df23489d98f86471fdb8c8ff" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" fillColor="#f6f5f4" alpha="64" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="24" y="96" width="284" height="41"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
          <sourceConnection id="id-65084328549848f0a1556784f0a149b5" lineWidth="2" lineColor="#1a5fb4" source="id-52f21087df23489d98f86471fdb8c8ff" target="id-09c0c02015a94757bd39a682fa512bf0" type="1"/>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-18c50d55929041b7aaef513a9753c5ab" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="148" y="108" width="156" height="25"/>
