        <documentation>Follow these steps to build your first report visually:

1. **Create a New View:** Right-click the **Tutorial** folder in your Views tree, select *New > ArchiMate View*, and name it `My First Document`. Open this blank canvas.
2. **Create the Root Artifact:** Drag a standard **Group** (Visual Group) onto your canvas. Make it large enough to hold other elements.
3. **Assign the Module:** In the Properties view, set the **Name** of this group to `Document`. This tells the engine to treat this container as the main wrapper.
4. **Set the Document Title:** Set the **Label Expression** of this group to `My First Document`.
5. **Nest a Chapter:** Drag a second **Group** and drop it *inside* the Document group to nest it spatially.
6. **Assign the Child Module:** Set the **Name** of this nested group to `Section`.
7. **Set the Chapter Heading:** Set the **Label Expression** of this nested group to `Hello World!`.
8. **Run the Script:** Ensure your newly created document structure is selected on the canvas and run the ArchiFabric script from your Scripts manager.
9. **Choose Save Location:** A system dialog box titled *Save ArchiFabric Document* will appear. Choose a folder on your computer and click Save.

When you open the generated PDF file, you will see a clean, formatted document containing your very first chapter titled **Hello World!**.</documentation>
        <property key="Lead" value="Let's put the visual engine into practice by creating a simple &quot;Hello World&quot; document. In this exercise, we will use two core Artifacts: a **Document** and a **Section**."/>
      </element>
