        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-fab7c20c1dfd42b59bee70ebc7ee8735" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="0" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="36" y="312" width="265" height="25"/>
          <feature name="lineStyle" value="3"/>
          <sourceConnection id="id-4fd3c1ab7ba046689c257ed1758c03f7" lineWidth="2" lineColor="#1a5fb4" source="id-fab7c20c1dfd42b59bee70ebc7ee8735" target="id-e6cb564e57c54ca6aaadef27673f9cfe" type="1">
            <bendpoint startX="384" endX="-122" endY="55"/>
          </sourceConnection>
          <content>Step 4. Link the Target</content>
        </child>
        <documentation>By placing our target view (`Deliver Customer Value`) right next to our Catalog template, ArchiFabric will automatically scan the target view, filter out all the Value Streams, and apply the layout we defined in the template to each of them.

**Follow these steps to apply the Catalog template:**

1. **Open your Document:** Go back to your `My First Document` canvas.
2. **Create a New Chapter:** To keep things organized, drag a new **Group** into your main `Document` wrapper, placing it below your previous work. Set its **Name** to `Section` and its **Label Expression** to `Value Streams`.
3. **Link the Template:** Drag your newly created `Value Stream Artifact` view from the model tree directly *inside* this new `Value Streams` section.
4. **Link the Target:** Drag the `Deliver Customer Value` view from the **Architecture** folder and drop it *inside* the exact same section, placing it right next to or below the template view. This combination forms our TargetStructure for the catalog.
5. **Generate the Output:** Run the ArchiFabric script again and save your file.

When you open the generated PDF, you will see a brand new chapter titled **Value Streams**. Below it, ArchiFabric has done the heavy lifting for you: it iterated through the `Deliver Customer Value` view, found the specific value streams (such as *Deliver Customer Solution* and *Support Customer*), and automatically generated a formatted sub-header and documentation paragraph for each of them!</documentation>
        <property key="Lead" value="Now that we have created our Catalog template (`Value Stream Artifact`), it is time to put it to work. We will use the exact same **TargetStructure** mechanism we learned in Section 4.5."/>
      </element>
