        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-56ebcb569f3244fb9a2fe962bd66221f" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" alpha="0" borderType="2">
          <bounds x="28" y="48" width="120" height="25"/>
          <content>Name:</content>
        </child>
        <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-1fe2bc1581ea4f5eb1aaa56a5661a0cc" font="1|Noto Sans|9.0|0|GTK|1|" textAlignment="1" borderType="1">
          <bounds x="148" y="48" width="156" height="25"/>
          <content>Catalog sort=position</content>
        </child>
        <documentation>In ArchiFabric, you can control an Artifact's behavior by adding specific parameters directly after its name in the Properties panel. A few powerful examples include `scope`, `select`, `class`, and `sort`.

For our catalog, we want the items to be displayed in the exact same order as they are visually arranged on the canvas (for example, from left to right, or top to bottom). To achieve this, we use the `sort=position` parameter.

**Follow these steps to sort your catalog logically:**

1. Open your template view named `Value Stream Artifact`.
2. Select the main `Catalog` group on your canvas.
3. In the Properties panel, change the **Name** of the group from `Catalog` to `Catalog sort=position`.
4. Save this template view.
5. Go back to your `My First Document` canvas. Ensure your document structure is selected and run the ArchiFabric script again.

When you open the new PDF, you will see that the generated list of Value Streams is now perfectly ordered. The Catalog engine has cleanly sorted the elements based on their physical geometry and position on your architecture canvas!</documentation>
        <property key="Lead" value="When reviewing the generated PDF from the previous section, you might notice that the Value Streams are listed, but perhaps not in the logical sequence you would expect. By default, ArchiFabric retrieves elements in the order they were originally created or stored in the underlying model. To structure the list logically, we use **Inline Parameters**."/>
      </element>
